            <ArticleTitle>Ca2+ leak-What is it? Why should we care? Can it be managed?</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1547-5271(17)31358-9</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.hrthm.2017.11.018</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>For arrhythmia triggers that are secondary to dysfunctional intracellular Ca2+ cycling, there are few, if any, agents that specifically target the Ca2+ handling machinery. However, several candidates have been proposed in the literature. Here we review the idea that these agents or their derivatives will prove invaluable in clinical applications in the future.</AbstractText>
